Installation Instructions
*************************

First, make sure you have CMake installed on your system.
You can check if CMake is installed by running the following command in your terminal:

cmake --version

If CMake is not installed, you can download it from the official website: https://cmake.org/download/

Extract the fatx package to a directory on your system.
Navigate to the directory that contains the extracted package using the terminal.
Create a new directory called "build". This directory will be used to store the build files generated by CMake.

mkdir build

Navigate to the build directory:

cd build

Run CMake on the package directory:

cmake /path/to/katx/package/directory

This command will generate the build files needed to build and install the package.
Once CMake has finished generating the build files, run the following command to build the package:

make

This command will build the package and create the necessary files for installation.
Finally, run the following command to install the package:

sudo make install

This command will install the package on your system. Note that you may need to run this command with root privileges (i.e., using sudo)
in order to install the package in certain system directories.
